' 34a The blocks of the N4 merge with an empty sibling: the empty block is
' the main parent of the merge block, so the merge adds the space branch to
' the state of an empty block.
'
' Source of the N4 figure of ../verification.md (section 34.9), a
' sub-figure of figure 34. The figure restates the test
' n4_space_merge_with_empty_sibling of casper/tests/reified/n4.rs and the
' three facts of Casper of decision 82. It adds no new fact.
'
' Changed on 2026-11-11 for the N4 condition of rrs-consensus-merge (a merge
' across blocks that contain every collection kind). The figure before showed
' a branch of two blocks (a queue and a set), the merge block and one touch of
' the queue. Now the branch has one creation block of each of the eight
' families, and one touch block follows the merge for each family.
'
' Reading order, from the bottom to the top:
'   1. Node 0, the leader, proposes the blocks C1 to C8 on genesis. Each block
'      creates the space of one family. Payer 0 offers C1, C3, C5 and C7, and
'      payer 1 offers C2, C4, C6 and C8.
'   2. Node 1 proposes the empty block E on genesis.
'   3. Node 2 receives C1 to C8 and E and proposes the merge block M. Its
'      first parent, the main parent, is E. The merge rejects no deploy.
'   4. Node 0 proposes the blocks T1 to T8 on M. Each block touches the space
'      of one family, with the payer that created the space. Every node
'      validates M and each touch block. At T8, every node reads the
'      deliveries of each family.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 34a-n4-merge-dag.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 34a-n4-merge-dag
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam RectangleBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
skinparam ranksep 24
title The blocks of the N4 merge with an empty sibling

rectangle "**T8**: payer 1 touches its cell space\nevery node reads the config, a take\nand a fired waiter of each family" as T8 $rrs_storage
rectangle "**T7**: payer 0 touches its stack space" as T7 $rrs_storage
rectangle "**T6**: payer 1 touches its bag space" as T6 $rrs_storage
rectangle "**T5**: payer 0 touches its PathMap space" as T5 $rrs_storage
rectangle "**T4**: payer 1 touches its VectorDB space" as T4 $rrs_storage
rectangle "**T3**: payer 0 touches its priority queue space" as T3 $rrs_storage
rectangle "**T2**: payer 1 touches its set space" as T2 $rrs_storage
rectangle "**T1**: node 0\npayer 0 touches its queue space" as T1 $rrs_storage
rectangle "**M**: merge block of node 2\nparents [E, C8]\nno rejected deploy" as M $rrs_host
rectangle "**C8**: payer 1 creates a cell space" as C8 $rrs_storage
rectangle "**C7**: payer 0 creates a stack space" as C7 $rrs_storage
rectangle "**C6**: payer 1 creates a bag space" as C6 $rrs_storage
rectangle "**C5**: payer 0 creates a PathMap space" as C5 $rrs_storage
rectangle "**C4**: payer 1 creates a VectorDB space" as C4 $rrs_storage
rectangle "**C3**: payer 0 creates a priority queue space" as C3 $rrs_storage
rectangle "**C2**: payer 1 creates a set space" as C2 $rrs_storage
rectangle "**C1**: node 0\npayer 0 creates a queue space\nwith records and a waiter" as C1 $rrs_storage
rectangle "**E**: node 1\nan empty block" as E $rrs_reserved
rectangle "**genesis**\noffered v6, three validators,\ntwo labeled payers" as G $rrs_host

T8 -[$rrs_relation]-> T7 : parent
T7 -[$rrs_relation]-> T6 : parent
T6 -[$rrs_relation]-> T5 : parent
T5 -[$rrs_relation]-> T4 : parent
T4 -[$rrs_relation]-> T3 : parent
T3 -[$rrs_relation]-> T2 : parent
T2 -[$rrs_relation]-> T1 : parent
T1 -[$rrs_relation]-> M : parent
M -[$rrs_effect,bold]-> E : main parent
M -[$rrs_relation,dashed]-> C8 : second parent
C8 -[$rrs_relation]-> C7 : parent
C7 -[$rrs_relation]-> C6 : parent
C6 -[$rrs_relation]-> C5 : parent
C5 -[$rrs_relation]-> C4 : parent
C4 -[$rrs_relation]-> C3 : parent
C3 -[$rrs_relation]-> C2 : parent
C2 -[$rrs_relation]-> C1 : parent
C1 -[$rrs_relation]-> G : parent
E -[$rrs_relation]-> G : parent

note right of M
The chains of the main parent never enter
a merge. With E as the main parent, the
merge applies the deploys of C1 to C8 to
the post-state of E, so the merge of the
space branch is not vacuous. Every node
validates M and each touch block.
end note

note right of C4
Leader rule: node 0 proposes every
space block. Each space has one payer,
and the two payers alternate. On the
merged base, a merge keeps the
sequential offers of one payer in one
branch (probe R10 of decision 108).
end note

note right of T4
Funding rule: each payer touches
only the spaces that it created.
end note

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_storage>    | block with a space deploy |
|<$rrs_host>       | genesis and the merge block |
|<$rrs_reserved>   | empty block |
**Arrows**
|<$rrs_effect>     | main parent: the merge starts from its post-state |
|<$rrs_relation>   | parent |
endlegend
@enduml
